<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified">
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
REQUEST schema for couponAuthentication (Customer360). This XML is carried in the form field
'XmlInput'. Audited 2026-10-12 against the loyalty-app service generation.

couponAuthentication is a read-only check: it reports whether a coupon code is usable at a
store. It does not consume the coupon (see couponPost).

Reading rules of the service:
  - Only the REQUEST child of the root is inspected; the root element name itself is not checked.
  - REQ_COUPON_DETAILS and REQ_TRANSACTION_DETAILS may appear in either order, as may their children.
  - Element names are case-sensitive.
  - When the tenant has a coupon prefix configured and enabled, a leading prefix is stripped
    from REQ_COUPON_CODE before lookup; the response still echoes the code as sent.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>
  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Top-level wrapper for the couponAuthentication request envelope.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="REQUEST">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>Request payload. Carries the coupon being authenticated and the transaction context in which it is presented.</xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:all>
              <xs:element name="REQ_COUPON_DETAILS">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Identifies the coupon to authenticate.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                  <xs:all>
                    <xs:element name="REQ_COUPON_CODE" type="xs:string">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The coupon code presented for authentication (as scanned or keyed at the POS). Missing or empty returns RESPONSE_CODE E116.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="REQ_COUPON_TYPE">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Coupon issuance model. Must equal the type of the promotion the coupon belongs to, otherwise the service returns RESPONSE_CODE E842 (also returned when this element is missing or empty). The value is echoed back as RESP_COUPON_TYPE. NOTE: the non-serialized value is NONSERIALIZE with no hyphen; the previously published value NON-SERIALIZE never matches and always yields E842.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:simpleType>
                        <xs:restriction base="xs:NMTOKEN">
                          <xs:enumeration value="SERIALIZE">
                            <xs:annotation>
                              <xs:documentation>Serialized coupons allow merchandisers to create large numbers of coupons with usage limits and randomly generated coupon codes in order to closely target and monitor coupon use.</xs:documentation>
                            </xs:annotation>
                          </xs:enumeration>
                          <xs:enumeration value="NONSERIALIZE">
                            <xs:annotation>
                              <xs:documentation>Non-serialized coupons: one shared code for the whole promotion.</xs:documentation>
                            </xs:annotation>
                          </xs:enumeration>
                        </xs:restriction>
                      </xs:simpleType>
                    </xs:element>
                  </xs:all>
                </xs:complexType>
              </xs:element>
              <xs:element name="REQ_TRANSACTION_DETAILS" minOccurs="0">
                <xs:annotation>
                  <xs:documentation>Transaction context in which the coupon is being authenticated. Optional: when REQ_STORE_ID is not supplied the service falls back to a default store of the tenant.</xs:documentation>
                </xs:annotation>
                <xs:complexType>
                  <xs:all>
                    <xs:element name="REQ_STORE_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>Store identifier, matched exactly as sent (no zero-padding is applied). An unknown store returns RESPONSE_CODE E127. When omitted or empty, a default store of the tenant is used. The coupon's promotion must be assigned to this store (otherwise E113).</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                    <xs:element name="REQUEST_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The date and time of this request. Accepted but not interpreted by the service (any text is tolerated); ISO 8601 is recommended, e.g. 2026-10-12T15:00:00Z. Coupon validity is always evaluated against the server clock.</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                    </xs:element>
                  </xs:all>
                </xs:complexType>
              </xs:element>
            </xs:all>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Retained from the earlier published schema. Not read by the service on requests; the tracking id is generated by the service and returned on the response.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
